00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:24.700
The real constraint is not the headline energy density number, but how quickly the new cells can be produced at acceptable yield and cost. Yield improvements directly affect how many usable cells leave the line each week, which in turn sets the pace for both vehicle production and megapack output. A modest gain and cell consistency can therefore unlock higher throughput without requiring additional factory floor space or new equipment purchases.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:40.980
Conventional lines treat cell manufacturing as a separate business from pack integration and final assembly. Tesla's structural pack approach collapses those stages, so a cell level gain can reduce the total number of parts and the labor hours required to build a pack.

